 the output with the same characters as the                 input.     -S          Start the output at a random spot in  the  input                 (default).   Note  that _t_r_a_v_e_s_t_y takes the input                 text to be wrapped around from the  end  to  the                 beginning.     -r_r_a_n_d      Set a particular integer  seed  for  the  random                 number  generator.   If  you  do not specify -_r,                 _t_r_a_v_e_s_t_y will choose a seed based on the current                 time.   It will print the seed on standard errorSun Release 4.0           Last change:                          1travesty(6)              GAMES AND DEMOS              travesty(6)                 if it receives an ALRM signal.DIAGNOSTICS     _f_a_t_a_l: _i_n_p_u_t _t_o_o _b_i_g          _t_r_a_v_e_s_t_y does not have  enough  memory  to  handle  the          input.RESTRICTIONS     _t_r_a_v_e_s_t_y cannot deal with ridiculously high orders or inputs     that cannot fit into memory.BUGS     None known.MACHINES     _t_r_a_v_e_s_t_y has been tested on  an  Astronautics  ZS-2  running     ZSUnix.VERSION     travesty version 1.1, dated 12/23/89.AUTHOR     Copyright 1989, Daniel J. Bernstein.SEE ALSO     kill(1)Sun Release 4.0           Last change:                          2